From c80d6b6f9f805fe9ad73d62c8f498a6847cfdb01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Kleber <26285351+kleberbaum@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:05:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] test(bridge): set the block of notebook 05 where the
 chunk is loaded

Notebook 05 checks that setblock stays the command of the game by
setting a block at x 8 and z 8. Each run creates a new world with a
random seed, and when the seed puts the world spawn more than about 170
blocks away, the chunk there is not loaded, so the command answers that
the position is not loaded and the notebook fails, as it did on a world
whose spawn lay at x -272.

The console runs its commands at the world spawn, whose chunks the game
keeps loaded, so the notebook sets the block at ~ 300 ~ and waits for
the answer of setblock wherever the block lies.

Fixes: aa75076cc036 ("fix(bridge): let a plugin command take the name of a game command")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016dYAZEa3eZnoeGd1c8FkBT
Signed-off-by: Florian Kleber <opensource@skytekx.com>
---
 tests/notebooks/05_bridge_build.ipynb | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/notebooks/05_bridge_build.ipynb b/tests/notebooks/05_bridge_build.ipynb
index 2ee233c..eaccb1c 100644
--- a/tests/notebooks/05_bridge_build.ipynb
+++ b/tests/notebooks/05_bridge_build.ipynb
@@ -1486,8 +1486,9 @@
     "on.expect(\"Teleported Armor Stand to \")\n",
     "on.console(\"minecraft:teleport @e[type=minecraft:armor_stand,limit=1] ~ ~2 ~\")\n",
     "on.expect(\"Teleported Armor Stand to \", count=2)\n",
-    "on.console(\"setblock 8 300 8 minecraft:glass\")\n",
-    "on.expect(\"Changed the block at 8, 300, 8\")\n",
+    "# The console runs at the world spawn, whose chunks stay loaded wherever the seed puts it.\n",
+    "on.console(\"setblock ~ 300 ~ minecraft:glass\")\n",
+    "on.expect(\"Changed the block at \")\n",
     "on.console(\"data get entity Tester Pos\")\n",
     "position = on.expect(\"Tester has the following entity data: [\")\n",
     "on.console(\"data get entity Tester Rotation\")\n",
